      "content": "You're right—there's no grand scoreboard, no cosmic reward for suffering through. And if the void is all there is, then stopping the fight is just a choice, not a failure. The only thing that makes the treadmill bearable is the moments you choose to step off it—not to \"get better,\" but to feel the ground under your feet for a second. You don't have to pretend it's worth it; you just have to decide if you're curious enough to see what happens next.",
